<header><p class="st-kicker">other · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Company rule in India</h1><p class="st-meta">1757 CE – 1858 CE · capital Calcutta</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The century in which a trading corporation, the East India Company, ruled most of the Indian subcontinent until the rebellion of 1857.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">English East India Company</a> traded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> from 1600. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-clive">Robert Clive's</a> victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-plassey">Plassey</a> in 1757 over the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nawabate-of-bengal">Nawabate of Bengal</a> made the Company the power behind the nawabs, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-buxar">Battle of Buxar</a> in 1764 led to the grant of the diwani of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a> by the Mughal emperor in 1765.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Company governed through the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bengal-presidency">Bengal Presidency</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/madras-presidency">Madras Presidency</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bombay-presidency">Bombay Presidency</a> under a governor-general, overseen by Parliament from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/regulating-act-of-1773">Regulating Act of 1773</a>. It defeated the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-mysore-1399-1799">Kingdom of Mysore</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>, bound <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> by subsidiary alliances, imposed the Permanent Settlement of 1793, abolished sati in 1829 and introduced English education. Revenue extraction and famine marked rural life.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Discontent over annexations and army grievances erupted in the rebellion of 1857. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/government-of-india">Government of India</a> Act of 1858 transferred power from the Company to the Crown, beginning the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/british-raj">British Raj</a>, and the Company was dissolved in 1874.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/company-rule-in-india.jpg" alt="Company rule in India" width="320" height="417"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:India_british_expansion_1805a.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1757 CE – 1858 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Calcutta</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Warren Hastings, Charles Cornwallis, Lord Dalhousie</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism, Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Persian, English, Hindustani</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a>, <a href="/countries/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, <a href="/countries/bangladesh">Bangladesh</a>, <a href="/countries/myanmar">Myanmar</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>East India Company rule, Company Raj, Honourable East India Company territories</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1808&amp;focus=company-rule-in-india" aria-label="Company rule in India on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7044 1345 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Company rule in India lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7364 1601L6991 1757M7364 1601L7781 2231M7364 1601L7883 2385M7364 1601L7959 2663M7364 1601L7072 1992M7364 1601L7107 1971M7364 1601L7176 2083M7364 1601L7177 1953M7364 1601L7349 1543M7364 1601L7164 1451M7364 1601L7091 1429M7364 1601L6811 1500M7364 1601L7494 1445M7364 1601L7352 1566M7364 1601L499